# ─── Source assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The pitch deck is ~94 MB — close to GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, and it
# would bloat history permanently. Everything in it is already in the site.
# Keep it wherever the team stores the deck (Drive, Dropbox, or Git LFS).
slides/

# Other large originals that belong outside the repo. Only the exported,
# web-sized files in assets/img/ should ever be committed.
*.psd
*.ai
*.sketch
*.fig
*.pdf
*.mov
*.mp4

# ─── OS cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── Editors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.history/

# ─── Local servers, logs, scratch ─────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.cache/
.tmp/
tmp/
_*.html

# ─── Secrets & environment ────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit these — a static site is fully public, including its repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Tooling, if any is added later ───────────────────────────────
# This site is plain HTML/CSS/JS with no build step. These entries just
# keep things clean if a formatter, bundler or link-checker shows up.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.parcel-cache/
.sass-cache/
*.css.map
*.js.map

# ─── GitHub Pages / Jekyll ────────────────────────────────────────
# .nojekyll is committed on purpose; these are Jekyll's own artifacts.
_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata
